From: enolagay@halcyon.com (Jason Johnson)
Date: Sun, 16 Oct 1994 11:54:10 -0800
Subject: [#94-10-259] Extropians Digest #94-10-197 - #94-10-220

"Jon 'Iain' Boone" states on Thu, 13 Oct 1994 12:39:51 -0400 (EDT)

>  I'd like to posit the idea that consciousness is an operational
>phenomenon -- if all of an entity's observable characteristcs match (within
>some degree of fuzziness) those of something which we assume is conscious,
>then that entity *is* conscious.
>
I agree, and would like to ad my two cents.

I believe consciousness to be a by-product of two of the minds properties.
Memory, or "Identity" and "perspective", meaning the perceptions and unique
point of view that is a function of a physical object (i.e. the brain).
Consciousness is not elusivly mystical, it is a by-product of an identity
and a perspective, a sum of it's parts.  If you preserve the Identity and
give it a new perspective, (i.e., up-loading) you give that being a new
consciousness.  That being is offspring.  If you can preserve the
perspective and the identity, that is immortality.  Both have value, and
both are desirable.

Through nanotechnology you could preserve your identity and perspective by
designing "nano-machines" to replicate and replace functioning brain cells,
prior to failure.  If they perfectly replaced each cell, your
"consciousness" could be perfectly preserved.  New nano-machines could
replace older ones prior to failure as well.  It would be a slow,
imperceptible evolution.  This to me, seems as about as immortal as you can
get.  We will be different then, but we always are changing, and change is
good.  What I was as a four-year old is dead now, and replaced with
something far better.  What I will be as a ten-thousand year old will be
vastly better, and what I am as a twenty-six year old will be dead.

Offspring.  Cloned copies, with downloaded identities could remain
soft-wired to the original, basically new limbs with unique identities, but
an intimate part of the original.  The limbs, though conscious, and capable
of their own government, could collect information and feed it back through
the soft-wires to both the master consciousness, and the other limbs
creating a much more efficient consciousness, capable of obtaining
information at higher rates of speed.  It would be a new consciousness far
broader and vastly superior to our simple and limited single perspective.
A single identity loved and shared by all it's perspectives.  You could
send your limbs off into space, or into strange new environments.  You
could take risks with you limbs while preserving you master consciousness.
You could experience amazing adventures, normally considered foolhardy, and
even experience death through your limbs.  Makes me wanna' quote the poet:
"Oh brave new world that has such people in it..."

If men cease to believe that they will one day become gods then they will
surely become worms. - Henry Miller



